      },
      "lineNbr": 471,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308473
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T08:53:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assume that each record represent different size but I can only know the average size for each record(12MB database, 6000 records, average size of record is 2k). If I just delete the number of record(1000 records) to meet the threshold, it might delete too much records. So I think the safe way was delete half of record first. Nevertheless, if we don\u0027t care about deleting too much  or all the records represent about the same size, we can simply calculate total number and delete them.",
      "parentUuid": "f311023c_d2c6faa7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 471,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 471,
        "endChar": 95
      },
      "revId": "ab89c6e34abe47ff14df9828cf419977bbbc6ccf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
