      "writtenOn": "2019-02-26T06:16:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need to interrupt the job here. Once you return from this method, the wakelock is not held any more and everything might start looking ugly.\n\nWhat that means for you is you need to have the maintenance code check for a stopping criterion reasonably often, and this should set that criterion. Ideally, you\u0027ll bound remaining execution time and join here with the background execution so that onStopJob does not return until the job is actually interrupted.",
